ils the attempt (it is retried like any other failure). Auto-detects from the lockfile: `pnpm-lock.yaml` -> `pnpm install --prefer-offline --frozen-lockfile`, `package-lock.json` -> `npm ci --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund`, a `package.json` with no lockfile -> `npm install --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund --no-package-lock`, no `package.json` -> no install. Pass `\"\"` to disable. Shares the agent's `--timeout`. Output goes to `<ticket>.install.log` |\n| `--max-turns <n>` | no | -- | Max agentic turns per agent run. Forwarded as `--max-turns <n>` to `claude` only; for `codex` and `pi` the flag is skipped with a warning and the agent runs with no turn limit. The limit is per spawn, not a total for the ticket: every retry and every re-spawn after a merge conflict starts with a fresh budget of `n` turns, so with `--retries 3` one ticket can use up to 4 x `n`. When omitted (or `0`), no limit is passed, so `--timeout` is the only cap. Takes precedence over the `[turns]` positional when both are given. Reaching the limit is an error exit, so the attempt fails and is retried like any other failure |\n| `--effort <level>` | no | -- | Starting effort/reasoning level. Each provider has its own ladder: `claude` supports `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max` (forwarded as `--effort`); `codex` supports `low`, `medium`, `high` (forwarded as `-c model_reasoning_effort=<level>`); `pi` supports `off`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max` (forwarded as `--thinking`). Omitted = provider default. Each retry steps up from here (see `--retries`) |\n| `--prefer-subagent <model>` | no | -- | `claude` only. Sets `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=<model>` for every claude agent redeye spawns (tickets, merge-conflict re-spawns, the reviewer and the fixer) and adds a prompt rule: hand read-only work (exploring the codebase, searching code, test runs with long output) to subagents, and make every edit and commit yourself. The reviewer gets the rule without the edit and commit line, since it never edits. `\"\"` is the same as omitting the flag. For `codex` and `pi` it is skipped with one warning at startup (`--prefer-subagent not supported by <provider>, skipping`). `--dry-run` prints `Prefer subagent: <model>`, or `(none)`. See [`--prefer-subagent` option](#--prefer-subagent-option) |\n| `--retries <n>` | no | `3` | Extra attempts per ticket after a failed run. Each retry starts from a fresh worktree and raises the effort level one rung (see Notes). `0` disables retries |\n| `--retry-delay <n>` | no | `30` | Seconds to wait before the first retry; doubles each further retry (30s, 60s, 120s, ...). `0` disables the wait |\n| `--concurrency <n>` | no | `5` | Max agents running at once within a wave. A wave with more ready tickets than this runs them through a pool: as one agent exits, the next ticket starts. The wave still finishes fully before its branches are merged |\n\n\n### Notes\n\n\n        const { stdout, stderr } = await spawnCli([\n            '--spec', FEAT,\n            '-m', 'opus',\n            '--timeout', '10',\n            '--test-cmd', 'true',\n            '--retries', '0',\n            '--no-review',\n        ], {\n            cwd: projectDir,\n            env: rolesEnv({ FAKE_CLAUDE_DELEGATE: MOCK_PASS }),\n            closeStdin: true,\n        })\n\n        const all = stdout + stderr\n        t.equal(all.split('same model').length - 1, 1,\n            'warns once about the same model')\n        t.notEqual(integrationBranches(projectDir), '',\n            'the run went ahead and created its branch')\n    } finally {\n        removeWorktreesAndRepo(projectDir)\n        rmSync(logDir, { recursive: true, force: true })\n        rmSync(templateDir, { recursive: true, force: true })\n    }\n})\n\ntest('CLI subprocess - an open review finding leaves the ticket ' +\n    'unresolved, unmerged and blocking its dependent; exit 1',\nasync t => {\n    const { projectDir, issuesDir, templateDir } = cliGitRepo()\n    const logDir = tmp()\n    try {\n        writeFileSync(\n            join(issuesDir, '01-task.md'),\n            makeTicketBody({ status: 'ready-for-agent' })\n        )\n        writeFileSync(\n            join(issuesDir, '02-after.md'),\n            makeTicketBody({ status: 'ready-for-agent', blockers: [1] })\n        )\n        // maxRounds 1: a single review decides the outcome\n        writeFileSync(\n            join(projectDir, '.redeye.json'),\n            JSON.stringify({\n                adversarial: {\n                    implement: FAKE_CLAUDE,\n                    review: FAKE_PI,\n                    maxRounds: 1,\n                    minRounds: 1,\n                },\n            })\n        )\n        commitAll(projectDir, 'add tickets and config')\n\n        const argvLog = join(logDir, 'argv.log')\n        const { code, stdout, stderr } = await spawnCli([\n            '--spec', FEAT,\n            '--timeout', '10',\n            '--test-cmd', 'true',\n            '--retries', '1',\n            '--no-review',\n        ], {\n            cwd: projectDir,\n            env: rolesEnv({\n                FAKE_CLAUDE_DELEGATE: MOCK_PASS,\n                FAKE_CLAUDE_ARGV_LOG: argvLog,\n                FAKE_PI_RESPONSES: 'finding',\n                FAKE_PI_COUNTER: join(logDir, 'counter'),\n            }),\n            closeStdin: true,\n        })\n        const all = stdout + stderr\n\n        t.equal(code, 1, 'exits 1: ' + all)\n        t.equal(readArgvLog(argvLog).length, 1,\n            'only ticket 01 ran, once: not retried, 02 never ran')\n\n        const integration = integrationBranches(projectDir)\n        const status = (name:string) => {\n            const body = gitOut(projectDir, [\n                'show', `${integration}:.scratch/${FEAT}/issues/${name}`,\n            ])\n            return /\\*\\*Status:\\*\\*\\s*(\\S+)/.exec(body)?.[1]\n        }\n        t.equal(status('01-task.md'), 'ready-for-human',\n            'the unresolved ticket is ready-for-human')\n        t.equal(status('02-after.md'), 'ready-for-agent',\n            'the dependent is untouched')\n        t.ok(all.includes('02-after.md'),\n            'the dependent is reported')\n\n        const changed = gitOut(projectDir, [\n            'log', integration, '--name-only', '--format=',\n        ])\n        t.ok(!changed.includes('mock-agent-change-'),\n            'the ticket change is not merged')\n        const branches = gitOut(projectDir, [\n            'branch', '--list', '--format=%(refname:short)',\n        ]).split('\\n')\n        t.ok(branches.some(b => b.includes('01-task') &&\n            b !== integration), 'the ticket branch is kept')\n        const worktrees = gitOut(projectDir, [\n            'worktree', 'list', '--porcelain',\n        ]).split('\\n').filter(l => l.startsWith('worktree '))\n        t.equal(worktrees.length, 1, 'the ticket worktree is removed')\n\n        const progress = gitOut(projectDir, [\n            'show', `${integration}:.scratch/${FEAT}/progress.md`,\n        ])\n        const progressFile = join(logDir, 'progress.md')\n        writeFileSync(progressFile, progress)\n        const entry = readProgress(progressFile)?.tickets.find(\n            p => p.filename === '01-task.md'\n        )\n        t.equal(entry?.done, false, 'progress.md records 01 as not done')\n    } finally {\n        removeWorktreesAndRepo(projectDir)\n        rmSync(logDir, { recursive: true, force: true })\n        rmSync(templateDir, { recursive: true, force: true })\n    }\n})","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WrySknwAs3JQJyjTpAwBj3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
