{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFMrNd5D9PQBUczBFj5N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six checklist items for ticket 05 now pass. I didn't need to change anything in `src/`: the fix rounds, verdicts, disputes and round limits were already on the branch from earlier commits. This ticket's work was test gaps and docs. `npm run build && npm test` exits 0 with no failing tests, and lint is clean.\n\n**Main gap fixed.** The mock fixer's `pass` mode only marks `[x] mock finding one`, which never matches the fake pi reviewer's finding. So no test had ever recorded a `fixed` response from the fixer. That includes the existing \"fixer marks `[x]` but reviewer keeps it open\" test, which wasn't testing what its name says. I added a `fix-all` mode to `test/mock-agent-review.js` that marks every finding in its prompt. With it, the new assertion failed before the change and passes after.\n\n**Tests per item.** Four items had tests already, so I strengthened them in `test/review-integration.test.ts`. Item 3 had no exit-code check, so it got a new CLI test in `test/integration.test.ts`. Apart from item 1 and the `[x]` test, every new check passed on its first run, which means they were written after the behaviour existed, not before. The notes file records this.\n\n1. **Fix then confirm:** round 1 records `fixed`, a passing test result and a new branch head. Round 2 reviews that head, and both the change and the fix land on main.\n2. **Dispute then withdraw:** round 1 records `disputed` with the reason from the notes file, and the next reviewer's prompt includes that reason. The ticket merges.\n3. **Dispute kept until `maxRounds`:** the new CLI test checks exit 1, `ready-for-human`, nothing merged, the branch kept, and the fixer running only once. It also checks the committed log: `disputed`, then `still-open`, then `unresolved`.\n4. **`minRounds: 2`:** the ticket merges after two clean reviews and no fixer runs.\n5. **Fixer keeps failing tests:** there are exactly 4 fix runs (2 fix attempts in each of 2 ticket attempts), the retried fixes see the previous test failure, both attempts end `failed` with `done:false`, and nothing merges.\n6. **`[x]` stays open:** the fixer marks the finding, the reviewer keeps it `still-open`, and the finding goes back to the fixer.\n\n**Docs.** The README's `.redeye.json` section now covers the round steps, the fixer contract, the rule that only the reviewer closes a finding, and what each log entry records. AGENTS.md has a short note on the mock fixer modes.\n\nTwo existing problems I saw but left alone:\n- The finish summary for an unresolved ticket reads \"0 completed, 1 failed, 1 need a human\". It looks like the unresolved ticket is also counted as failed.\n- `tsc --noEmit` reports existing type errors in the test files, for example display stubs that lack `setRoundLabel`. The suite still runs because esbuild doesn't type-check.\n\nMy notes for this attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":128588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"863441ca-d33f-471b-aa58-a41aeaae5b37","uuid":"437f1cdb-11c0-4afb-b8a8-03b63e5127b7","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:26:15.653Z","request_id":"req_011ChFMrN7p2AoE1yL1z1LUw"}
